error[consumed_borrowed_handle]: `g5_close` ends the life of what it is given, and `h` was borrowed — this function promised not to change it
  at tests/golden/full/fixedbugs-2242-through-the-dot-the-at-goes-on-the-function-that-borrowed.hero:18:12
     |
  18 |     return h.g5_close()  #~ consumed_borrowed_handle
     |            ^
  note: a parameter written without `@` is borrowed: the caller keeps the value and reads it again after the call, so a call that frees it leaves them holding an address C has taken back. Write the parameter `@h` in the signature of `closed` and `@` before its argument at every call of `closed`, which says on both lines that the value does not survive; this call stays as it is, since `g5_close` takes this argument without `@`
  note: this refuses the call, not the copy: a copy made BEFORE the call still holds the freed address, and nothing here sees that. design.md Part 8 wart 20 states that cost and names what would close it

